","y":2020,"p":"Bishkek","s":"protests in response to the 2020 Kyrygz Parliamentary Election","x":"The 2020 Kyrgyz Revolution, also known as the Third Kyrgyz Revolution, began on 5 October 2020, in response to the previous day's parliamentary election that was perceived by protestors as unfair, with allegations of electoral fraud. The results of the election were annulled on 6 October 2020. Outcome: President Jeenbekov resigns; Prime Minister Kubatbek Boronov resigns; Parliamentary Speaker Dastan Jumabekov resigns; Election results annulled on 6 October 2020; Former president Atambayev freed from jail; Mass looting in Bishkek on 8 October 2020; State of emergency declared in Bishkek; The Armed Forces of Kyrgyzstan deploy across the capital. Cost: Dead: 1 protester; Injured: 1,000+.","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q99979519"],["BBC","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-54422884"],["Mediazona","https://mediazona.ca/online/2020/10/07/opposition-3#36253"],["Al Jazeera","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2020/10/8/kremlin-says-kyrgyzstan-is-in-chaos-and-needs-stabilising"],["Eurasianet","https://eurasianet.org/kyrgyzstan-taking-power-one-building-at-a-time"],["Illiberalism Studies Program Working Papers","https://www.illiberalism.org/populism-la-kyrgyz-sadyr-japarov-nationalism-anti-elite-sentiment-kyrgyzstan/"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Kyrgyz_Revolution"]]},{"c":3,"k":7,"t":"COVID-19 pandemic in Kyrgyzstan","w":"from 18 March 2020","y":2020,"p":"Kyrgyzstan","s":"viral pandemic in Kyrgyzstan","o":"COVID-19 pandemic by country and territory","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q87902950"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_Kyrgyzstan"]],"u":7},{"c":3,"k":7,"t":"COVID-19 pandemic in Asia","w":"from 1 December 2019","y":2019,"p":"Asia","s":"ongoing COVID-19 viral pandemic in Asia","o":"COVID-19 pandemic","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q86521237"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikiped